WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.700
- This is a topic I've
been meaning to address

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:04.680
for a long period of time,

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.100
but I had an isolated incident
happen to me on TikTok

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.720
that I think is very emblematic

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.640
of what's happening on social media,

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:16.200
specifically within the
healthcare or medical community

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:19.170
that I find to be very, very problematic.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:21.780
And I wanna say on the
outset of this video

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:24.510
this is not intended to attack anybody.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:27.750
There's gonna be a reason why
we cut out everyone's names

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.640
out of the video, their usernames,

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:33.570
because the purpose of this is
to get the medical community

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:35.400
on the same page,

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.220
to make sure that we improve
our communication style,

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:43.220
myself included and learn from
situations just like this one

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:47.220
in order to facilitate the message

00:00:47.220 --> 00:00:48.933
of greater good or public health.

00:00:51.216 --> 00:00:53.640
A month ago, I posted a short,
a cutdown of my interview

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.730
with Sebastian Maniscalco
on the topic of RSV.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:58.050
Right now with RSV,

00:00:58.050 --> 00:00:59.790
one of the leading theories of why

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:01.860
there's such a run on hospitals is because

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.380
generally kids get RSV in their
first three years of life.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:05.970
There's like a 50% chance each year

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:07.260
that they get their first episode.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:09.630
And their first episode with
RSV is usually the worst.

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.400
The time that where they
need breathing treatments

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.540
maybe ICU stay.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.940
And we've held our kids back from school

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:17.220
grandparents and everybody
that could've gotten them sick

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:18.600
for the last two years.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.520
So now the children
that would've gotten it

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.530
each year have all gotten
it at the same time

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:23.490
and it was their first time.

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:25.320
So it kind of creates a run on hospitals.

00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:26.340
That's the leading theory.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:28.470
RSV is a respiratory virus

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:30.540
that actually affects people of all ages,

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:31.860
but it happens to be worse

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.840
in the very young and the elderly.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:35.730
What's been going on in our communities

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:38.910
is that we've seen higher
rates of hospitalization

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:43.050
for children with RSV over the last season

00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:46.230
which means basically starting
late October, November.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:48.990
And we had some theories circulating

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:51.090
as to why that was going on.

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:53.970
I presented one of the leading theories

00:01:53.970 --> 00:01:56.219
and I specify one of the leading theories

00:01:56.219 --> 00:02:00.137
very strongly here
because I largely believe,

00:02:00.137 --> 00:02:03.990
as a physician myself,
who treats children,

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.540
that this is a multifactorial situation.

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:08.610
Meaning that there's
probably multiple factors

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:10.560
and multiple theories that are to be true.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.360
And each of them have holes

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:14.190
because they do not on their own.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:17.700
Explain the given spike
in RSV hospitalizations.

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:21.270
The theory of COVID
co-infection, fluid co-infection,

00:02:21.270 --> 00:02:24.270
and immune dysregulation, partially true.

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:26.834
The fact that the timing
has been thrown off

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:28.320
and our seasonal patterns
have been thrown off.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.920
The fact that pregnant patients

00:02:30.857 --> 00:02:33.591
weren't exposed to RSV while pregnant,

00:02:33.591 --> 00:02:37.034
therefore transfer less
protection for newborns,

00:02:37.034 --> 00:02:38.250
partially true.

00:02:38.250 --> 00:02:40.650
The one that I presented,
spoke to the fact

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:44.058
that children over the
last two years or so

00:02:44.058 --> 00:02:46.530
had less exposure to RSV

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:49.110
because we were protecting
them from COVID.

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:52.530
We were not having normal activities,

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:54.000
normal interactions,

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.280
their siblings were not going to school,

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.110
their parents were not going to work,

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:01.380
and as a result, they, they
had less exposure to RSV.

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.063
When you have less exposure,

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:06.060
you are less likely to get RSV.

00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:09.510
And children who get
RSV for the first time

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:12.240
usually get a worse case of RSV.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:14.790
I wasn't saying anything about
children's immune systems.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.740
I wasn't saying anything about

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:19.290
our mitigation methods for COVID.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:20.640
I was simply saying that

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:22.650
because they had less exposure to RSV,

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:26.070
that more children were
exposed to RSV this season

00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:28.140
as we're going back to regular life.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.100
And as a result,

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.840
more of them were getting
it for their first time,

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:32.250
which means more severe cases.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.530
So it's basically just a timing issue.

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:36.300
Nothing to do with the strength

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.580
or weakness of their immune systems.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:42.833
In fact, this theory about
the timing being thrown off

00:03:42.833 --> 00:03:45.330
was not my theory.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:48.336
It happens to be one
of the leading theories

00:03:48.336 --> 00:03:52.530
that was spoken in news by New
York Presbyterian Hospital.

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:54.150
It was on ABC news.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.460
Doctors on NPR talked about this.

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:58.650
Dr. McGeer from University of Toronto

00:03:58.650 --> 00:04:00.480
said it perfectly in this interview.

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:01.710
- There's no question in my mind

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:06.710
that the biggest impact of
this excess in illness in kids

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:11.730
and in our ICUs, is related to the fact

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:14.557
that kids just weren't exposed to RSV.

00:04:16.818 --> 00:04:17.651
- After posting this TikTok,

00:04:17.651 --> 00:04:19.996
I got comments from other doctors

00:04:19.996 --> 00:04:24.090
who were debating the
validity of this theory

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:25.390
whether this is the theory

00:04:26.294 --> 00:04:28.080
that explains the recent spike in RSV

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.240
and some of their arguments were right.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.040
I actually agreed with their arguments.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.080
They were saying that in Sweden

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.360
they did not have a strict of a lockdown,

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:38.250
and yet they're still having this spike.

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:39.540
Why is that the case?

00:04:39.540 --> 00:04:41.220
And I'm not an expert
on Sweden, by the way.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:44.070
I don't know exactly what their
healthcare system is like.

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:45.450
So I don't even pretend to know that.

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.340
One of the theories going around right now

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:50.250
is about COVID immune
system dysregulation.

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:52.020
That some doctors believe,

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:54.930
that all these children that
have had COVID in the past

00:04:54.930 --> 00:04:56.520
have a weakened immune system.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:59.310
Therefore, as a result,
RSV affects them more.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:00.990
There may be some truth in this

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:05.160
because any co-infection whether
we're talking about COVID,

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:09.300
flu, rhinovirus these
types of co-infections

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:12.510
can make your immune
system have fluctuations

00:05:12.510 --> 00:05:14.580
in its ability to fight other viruses.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.320
So that's partially true.

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:18.720
There's some even data showing

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:21.150
that some immune cells are impacted

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:22.650
by having COVID in the past

00:05:22.650 --> 00:05:25.950
the concept of immunity debt has popped up

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:29.656
among certain circles, where they believe

00:05:29.656 --> 00:05:32.970
having children protected from exposure

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:36.090
has led them to have a
weakened immune system.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:38.490
And this is not what I was saying.

00:05:38.490 --> 00:05:41.010
This is not how immune systems work.

00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:43.950
Yes, there is a hygiene
theory that long term,

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:46.590
chronically, over the course of our lives,

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:49.740
if we hyper protect
ourselves from bacteria

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:52.830
and constantly disinfect everything

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:55.890
it could have a meaningful
impact of our lives.

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:58.290
But over the course of one or two years

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:02.340
protecting children from a
serious situation like COVID

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:04.200
that initially we knew very little about

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:06.390
and then we learned more
and it was very scary

00:06:06.390 --> 00:06:08.400
and our hospital systems were overwhelmed

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.890
will not impact their immune system

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:12.930
so much so that they're weakened.

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:14.490
That is not what I was saying.

00:06:14.490 --> 00:06:17.463
And anyone pushing that is inaccurate.

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:20.220
To my disappointment,

00:06:20.220 --> 00:06:24.720
this past week, I started
seeing an increase

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:28.680
of attacks from other
medical professionals

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:31.260
on this TikTok that I did not expect.

00:06:31.260 --> 00:06:33.270
Because I totally see how we can debate

00:06:33.270 --> 00:06:36.120
what is the reason for this RSV spike.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:38.130
But I started seeing personal attacks.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:40.620
In fact, there was one
comment that upset me

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:42.847
because the person came in and said,

00:06:42.847 --> 00:06:46.027
"Wow you pretend to be a
so-called "doctor." in quotes.

00:06:46.027 --> 00:06:48.871
"Here's an immunologist's perspective."

00:06:48.871 --> 00:06:50.880
And it was like a personal attack

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:53.220
on me as if I'm not a real
doctor, treating patients.

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:55.740
When I have RSV patients,
I have COVID patients.

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:58.890
I give guidance. I strive to
be the best doctor that I can.

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:00.750
I've tried to be an accurate voice

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:03.226
with evidence-based medicine
throughout the pandemic

00:07:03.226 --> 00:07:06.030
and to have this doctor
do a personal attack on me

00:07:06.030 --> 00:07:07.350
to upset me, so I blocked them.

00:07:07.350 --> 00:07:09.540
In fact, that was one of
my New Year's resolutions

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:11.790
to try and not pay attention

00:07:11.790 --> 00:07:13.390
to the negative comments as much

00:07:14.308 --> 00:07:15.780
that I don't feel are reflective
of who I am as a person

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:17.490
and block and move on.

00:07:17.490 --> 00:07:19.470
But when I blocked said person,

00:07:19.470 --> 00:07:22.380
they created content around
the fact that I blocked them

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:25.080
as if I was silencing their medical voice.

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:27.390
That I am a medical grifter,

00:07:27.390 --> 00:07:31.671
that I am the same as Dr. Oz
in fueling misinformation,

00:07:31.671 --> 00:07:33.840
which is so disheartening

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:37.380
because the whole reason
this YouTube channel exists,

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:39.600
is to put out evidence-based medicine.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:42.823
So to be accused of spreading it myself

00:07:42.823 --> 00:07:46.080
just kills me because it doesn't
make a lot of sense to me.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:48.423
Why are, are people doing this?

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:51.210
Some of the negative comments

00:07:51.210 --> 00:07:55.980
pointed out that I was
blocking and deleting comments

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:57.690
from people who disagreed

00:07:57.690 --> 00:07:59.820
with this theory that I was presenting.

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:01.800
And that's not the case.

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:03.780
I believe in healthy discourse and debate

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:04.863
we need more of it.

00:08:05.827 --> 00:08:06.900
It just needs to stay respectful

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:09.450
because the only reason I blocked

00:08:09.450 --> 00:08:11.250
the individual I mentioned earlier

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:14.070
was they started personally
attacking me in life.

00:08:14.070 --> 00:08:16.920
If you ever want to have
a meaningful conversation

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:18.300
or even a debate with someone,

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:20.130
you can't start it off by saying,

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:22.080
so you're a so-called doctor

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:24.900
or call them a name and hope
that they're gonna listen.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.870
These same people who say these things

00:08:27.870 --> 00:08:31.770
about me and attack me also
have been attacked themselves

00:08:31.770 --> 00:08:32.880
and know what it feels like.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:35.030
So we have to approach
this empathetically.

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:37.680
We need to do a better job

00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:41.370
in social media when it comes
to healthcare communication.

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:44.550
These are still sort of hurdles
that we need to get across

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:47.610
as communicators when it comes
to a public health setting.

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:49.650
And I think it's really important

00:08:49.650 --> 00:08:51.330
that we move away from toxicity

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:52.800
within the medical community.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:56.010
'Cause otherwise what happens
is it fractures our ability

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:57.450
to educate people.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:09:01.020
We fuel tribalism, we lead people

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:03.150
more confused than educated.

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:05.190
They feel like this
person knows the answer

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:07.020
and this person's evil, this person's bad.

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:08.730
And this type of dichotomy

00:09:08.730 --> 00:09:11.220
this black or white thinking is unhealthy

00:09:11.220 --> 00:09:14.520
because medicine is not a
hundred percent science.

00:09:14.520 --> 00:09:15.900
There is an art to it.

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:17.730
There are individual distinctions

00:09:17.730 --> 00:09:19.530
that need to be made per patient.

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:21.990
That's why generalized
medicine is not the same

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:25.080
as what is accurate for the
person sitting in front of you.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:28.470
So please, doctors online,

00:09:28.470 --> 00:09:31.230
I know that we've been attacked

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:32.730
throughout the last few years

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:34.890
for putting out accurate information.

00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:39.890
We have seen a rise, a tremendous
rise in misinformation.

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:44.910
But do not lead this to
create displacement anger

00:09:44.910 --> 00:09:46.860
on other physicians or other individuals

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:49.920
or even your patients who may say things

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:53.580
that you disagree with you
may find slightly inaccurate.

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.920
Because the more we attack

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:58.950
and the more we label
everything as misinformation,

00:09:58.950 --> 00:10:01.080
the more it takes away our ability

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:04.170
to be true fact checkers and educators.

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:06.870
I'm actually such a fan of healthy debate.

00:10:06.870 --> 00:10:08.850
I love it when people
tell me that I'm wrong

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:11.100
and have a meaningful discussion with me.

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:13.170
You've told me I've
been wrong several times

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:16.080
and here's a full video
with all the mistakes

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:18.330
that I've made in my videos
over the last few years.

00:10:18.330 --> 00:10:19.530
I hope you enjoy it

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:22.023
and I hope as always, you
stay happy and healthy.

